---
export const prerender = true;
import '../styles/global.css';

const OBJECTIONS = [
  {
    id: 'credit',
    q: "Won't opening new cards trash my credit score?",
    a: "Short term: a 5-10 point dip from the inquiry — it's real, and we won't pretend it isn't. Long term: your score usually climbs. More accounts = higher total credit limit = lower utilization ratio. We teach you to pace applications so you never trigger a velocity flag. Most of our users see their score go up within 90 days.",
    icon: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="23 6 13.5 15.5 8.5 10.5 1 18"/><path d="M17 6h6v6"/></svg>`
  },
  {
    id: 'debt',
    q: "I don't want to get into debt chasing points.",
    a: "You shouldn't. Carrying a balance wipes out every dollar of value from rewards in days. Our spend pacing tool keeps you inside your existing budget — we never recommend spending more than you already do. No balance. No interest. If you can't pay it off monthly, we'll tell you to wait.",
    icon: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>`
  },
  {
    id: 'spend',
    q: "I don't spend thousands a month. Can I even hit these bonuses?",
    a: "$1,000/month on groceries, gas, and insurance gets you most starter bonuses. We show you how to time your application around expenses you already have — car insurance renewal, back-to-school, holiday shopping — so you hit the goal without spending a single extra dollar. You already earn these points. You just aren't collecting them.",
    icon: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="8" cy="21" r="1"/><circle cx="19" cy="21" r="1"/><path d="M2.05 2.05h2l2.66 12.42a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.58h9.78a2 2 0 0 0 1.95-1.57l1.65-7.43H5.12"/></svg>`
  },
  {
    id: 'complex',
    q: "This sounds incredibly complicated. I don't have time to learn all of this.",
    a: "The learning curve is why we exist. Our Dream Trip Engine gives you one checklist: your airport, your destination, which card, when to apply, how to book. You follow the steps. We did the research. The average user goes from zero to a booked award itinerary without reading a single points blog.",
    icon: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="8" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"/><line x1="8" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"/><line x1="8" y1="18" x2="21" y2="18"/><line x1="3" y1="6" x2="3.01" y2="6"/><line x1="3" y1="12" x2="3.01" y2="12"/><line x1="3" y1="18" x2="3.01" y2="18"/></svg>`
  },
  {
    id: 'regional',
    q: "I fly out of McAllen or Laredo. Deals are only for DFW, right?",
    a: "This is the biggest myth in travel hacking — and it costs Texas regional flyers thousands every year. Award prices are often zone-based, not distance-based. A flight from MFE to London can cost the same points as one from DFW. We track these arbitrage windows specifically. Regional hubs are an advantage, not a limitation.",
    icon: `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 10c0 6-8 12-8 12s-8-6-8-12a8 8 0 0 1 16 0Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>`
  }
];
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>The Skeptic's Guide to Texas Travel Hacking</title>
  <meta name="description" content="No hype, no fluff. Just the math and logic of how travel hacking actually works for Texas regional flyers." />
  <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>🛡️</text></svg>" />
  <!-- Fonts (async — non-blocking) -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://api.fontshare.com">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800;900&display=swap" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=satoshi@900,700,500,300,400&display=swap" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
  <noscript>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800;900&display=swap">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=satoshi@900,700,500,300,400&display=swap">
  </noscript>
  <!-- Google Analytics -->
  <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-XSTNVD0CLC"></script>
  <script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
    gtag('js', new Date());
    gtag('config', 'G-XSTNVD0CLC');
  </script>
</head>

<body class="bg-primary text-primary font-body selection:bg-tcf-aviation-blue/30 selection:text-white">

  <!-- Nav -->
  <nav class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 px-6 py-5 glass border-b border-white/5">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-3 no-underline group">
        <div class="p-2 rounded-xl bg-tcf-aviation-blue/10 border border-tcf-aviation-blue/20">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="text-tcf-aviation-blue"><path d="M17.8 19.2 16 11l3.5-3.5C21 6 21.5 4 21 3c-1-.5-3 0-4.5 1.5L13 8 4.8 6.2c-.5-.1-.9.1-1.1.5l-.3.5c-.2.5-.1 1 .3 1.3L9 12l-2 3H4l-1 1 3 2 2 3 1-1v-3l3-2 3.5 5.3c.3.4.8.5 1.3.3l.5-.2c.4-.3.6-.7.5-1.2z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <span class="font-black text-lg uppercase tracking-tight text-white">Texas Cheap Flights</span>
      </a>
      <div class="hidden lg:flex items-center gap-8">
        {[
          { label: "The Strategy", href: '/#how-it-works' },
          { label: "Past Deals", href: '/past-deals' },
        ].map(link => (
          <a href={link.href} class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors no-underline">{link.label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a href="/#waitlist" class="btn-primary" style="padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; font-size: 0.875rem;">
        Join the Waitlist
      </a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <header class="text-center mb-20 anim-fade-up">
        <span class="label text-gold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold text-xs mb-6 inline-block">The Honest Breakdown</span>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl mb-8 text-white font-black leading-tight">
          The Skeptic's Guide to <span class="text-gold">Texas Points</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          You've probably heard this is complicated, risky, or only for big spenders.<br/><span class="text-white font-bold">It's not.</span> Here's the math — no gurus, no hype, no hidden catch.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Objections List — front-loaded -->
      <section class="space-y-12 mb-32">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-center text-white mb-16">Common Objections, Answered.</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-8">
          {OBJECTIONS.map(obj => (
            <div id={obj.id} class="liquid-glass p-8 md:p-12 rounded-[2.5rem] border-white/5 hover:border-white/20 transition-all duration-300">
              <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8">
                <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl bg-tcf-gold/10 flex items-center justify-center text-tcf-gold flex-shrink-0" set:html={obj.icon}></div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4 tracking-tight">{obj.q}</h3>
                  <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-body">{obj.a}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Math Section -->
      <section class="mb-32">
        <div class="liquid-glass p-10 md:p-16 rounded-[3rem] relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute -top-20 -left-20 w-64 h-64 bg-tcf-aviation-blue/10 blur-[120px] rounded-full"></div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black mb-10 text-white">Rule #1: This is not "Free."</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-400 mb-8 leading-relaxed text-lg font-body">
            Good. Now here's why this actually works — and why the banks designed it this way. You aren't getting anything for free. You are performing a service for the banks.
          </p>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10">
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <h3 class="text-white font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-tcf-aviation-blue/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] text-tcf-aviation-blue">1</span>
                Customer Acquisition
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 leading-relaxed font-body">
                Banks spend billions to find reliable customers. They would rather give YOU 60,000 points (worth ~$900) than spend $900 on a generic TV ad. You are just a high-value customer being 'acquired.'
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <h3 class="text-white font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-tcf-aviation-blue/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] text-tcf-aviation-blue">2</span>
                Interchange Fees
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 leading-relaxed font-body">
                Every time you buy a taco in San Antonio, the merchant pays a 2-3% fee. The bank keeps most of that — but when you use the right card, they give half of it back to you as points.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Rule #2: Cash Glitches -->
      <section class="mb-32">
        <div class="liquid-glass p-10 md:p-16 rounded-[3rem] relative overflow-hidden border border-red-500/10">
          <div class="absolute -top-20 -right-20 w-64 h-64 bg-red-500/5 blur-[120px] rounded-full"></div>
          <div class="relative z-10">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-500/10 border border-red-500/20 text-[9px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-red-400 mb-8 inline-block">
              ⚡ Algorithm Glitch
            </span>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-black mb-6 text-white">Rule #2: Cash Glitches Don't Care About Your Credit Score.</h2>
            <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed text-lg font-body">
              Not ready for the credit card strategy yet? Fine. We also scan for cash pricing errors — when an airline's algorithm misfires and sells a $1,200 roundtrip from Texas for $350. These windows are real, they happen every week, and they close fast. By the time it hits a deal blog, it's already patched. We send the alert the moment the bot goes rogue.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Texas Edge -->
      <section class="mb-32 text-center">
        <div class="p-12 md:p-20 rounded-[4rem] bg-tcf-gold/5 border border-tcf-gold/10 relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_center,_var(--tcf-gold)_0%,_transparent_20%)] opacity-10"></div>
          <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white mb-8">The Texas Sweet Spot Nobody Talks About</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8 font-body">
            Being landlocked in the middle of the country sounds like a disadvantage. It isn't. Award programs price routes by zone — not by how close you are to a hub. Texas regional flyers get access to the same international sweet spots as DFW, at the same point cost, with less competition for seats. We track every one of these windows from <span class="text-tcf-gold font-bold">MFE, LRD, BRO, and CRP</span>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-white font-bold mb-10">Still not convinced? See every deal we've actually found and sent — real routes, real prices, no cherry-picking.</p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <a href="/past-deals" class="btn-primary px-8 py-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 no-underline">
              See Real Past Deals
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </a>
            <a href="/#waitlist" class="text-tcf-gold font-bold text-sm hover:text-white transition-colors no-underline">
              Or join the waitlist →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="py-20 bg-tcf-navy-deep border-t border-white/5 text-center">
    <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
      © 2026 Texas Cheap Flights. No fluff, just math.
    </p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // Observe fade-up
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add('anim-fade-up');
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });

    document.querySelectorAll('.anim-fade-up, .liquid-glass').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
  </script>
</body>
</html>
